From b014a03161d1943ac8a968b6b24de3f54143e407 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:36:08 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Degoogle follow-ups: answer Safe Browsing checks at once,
 default it off, restore update_client

- SafeBrowsingApiBridge.startUriLookupBySafeBrowsingApi (cromite's
  Fix-chromium-vanilla) returned without answering native, so every
  response was held for the 5 s Safe Browsing throttle timeout and typed
  hostnames hit the 3 s HTTPS-upgrade timer first (ERR_TIMED_OUT, then
  the auto-reload succeeded). Answer FAILURE_HANDLER_NULL immediately;
  native then treats the API as unavailable. Cromite avoids this only via
  its dropped Modify-default-preferences (Safe Browsing off).
- kSafeBrowsingEnabled defaults to false: there is no backend, so the
  setting no longer claims protection that does nothing.
- components/update_client back to vanilla (POST body, no version-0
  skip, CUP signing on): cromite's Enable-component-updater changes only
  affected extension update checks here, since no component registers.
  Web Store extensions still do not auto-update (update URL stays
  about:blank); self-hosted update URLs work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
